                        "sense_id": "cb8fdb7f-04cb-300b-a3e8-fe0643fa0761",
                        "entry_id": "e1aa54ea-87f9-3e5f-a241-e871826d819e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "That portion of a parent's estate of which he cannot disinherit his children without a legal cause."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a10febb-37ef-407d-a89d-07432fd9bda5",
                                "sense_id": "cb8fdb7f-04cb-300b-a3e8-fe0643fa0761",
                                "text": "[…] when there is no testament; but this is not to be understood of persons to whom a legitime, or child's part, is due by law."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be80e97e-6802-4dd2-9aa8-c36e6b11839e",
                                "sense_id": "cb8fdb7f-04cb-300b-a3e8-fe0643fa0761",
                                "text": "[…] or of renouncing all testamentary advantage, and claiming his legitime only as secured to him by the law independent of the testament. But where the testator bequeaths to the forced heir nothing beyond his legitime, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "11130bbd-03f3-40b0-ad18-ec2b0ab187f3",
                                "sense_id": "cb8fdb7f-04cb-300b-a3e8-fe0643fa0761",
                                "text": "[W]here a compulsory heir and an heir not entitled to a legitime are institute to the entire state without designation of shares, the legitime should first be paid before the equal sharing is applied.\n[…]\nArticle 983 does not modify the rules on legitimes, the legitimes of LCDs and the surviving spouse (SS) shall always be first satisfied in preference to the illegitimate children and descendants (ICDs)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
